COMMON TRAPS

- ⚠️ Scalar Nature: Current has direction but is a scalar (it doesn't use vector addition).
- ⚠️ Resistance vs Resistivity: Resistivity does NOT change when wire is stretched; only Resistance changes.
- ⚠️ Potentiometer V: V_wire is not the EMF of the driver battery if there is internal resistance or a series rheostat.
- ⚠️ Series Bulbs: A 60W bulb glows brighter than a 100W bulb in series (because it has higher resistance).
- ⚠️ Ideal vs Real: Ideal ammeter (R=0); Ideal voltmeter (R=∞).
- ⚠️ Short Circuit: Zero-resistance wire in parallel with a resistor "kills" that resistor.
- ⚠️ Mass: In v_d = eEτ/m, 'm' is the mass of the electron, not the metal.

